<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1223–<a href="/years/1282">1282</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Llywelyn the Last</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd, known as Llywelyn the Last, was prince of Gwynedd and the only native ruler formally recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, by Henry III in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery">Treaty of Montgomery</a> in 1267. Conflict with Edward I led to English invasions in 1277 and 1282. He was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilmeri">Cilmeri</a> in December 1282, and Edward completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd.jpg" alt="Llywelyn ap Gruffudd" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Wriothesley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llywelyn_ap_Gruffudd,_Wriothesley_Garter_Book,_transparency.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
